<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output up 5.9 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output up 5.9 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (unadjusted) rose 5.9 percent in June after a 5.7 percent fall in May, and was 19.9 percent higher than in June 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Industrial output rose 10.7 percent in the January-June period against the same period of last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	 JUNE	MAY	  JUNE 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	  5.9     -5.7	     -5.9</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		 19.9	6.5 (6.6)	2.6</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)    36.0	N/A(28.4)	N/A</p>
<p> mining m/m change		  11.4     -9.0(-8.8)     -4.4</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		15.5     -0.9(-0.7)     -8.2</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	  6.7     -4.4(-4.3)     -5.6</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change     21.2	7.3		4.7</p>
<p> utilities m/m change	     -6.3    -15.5(-15.4)   -10.1</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	    9.6	5.2( 5.3)     -5.8</p>
<p>NOTES: Revised data in brackets. June 1997 had 22 working days, May had 21 and June 1996 had 20 working days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
